<description>&lt;p&gt;President de la Espriella opened a Colombian embassy in Jerusalem, prompting condemnation from Pakistan and other Muslim states, while he also announced a cultural counterrevolution against &amp;quot;wokeism&amp;quot; and ordered the removal of over thirty artworks from the National Museum. Opposition groups protested his budget cuts that threaten the peace tribunal and searches for the disappeared, and the peace tribunal charged former FARC members with anti-Indigenous crimes. An acid-attack survivor cancelled planned euthanasia after a public appeal, and a preacher was killed by a criminal group in Cartagena. 225 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuAFBVV95cUxObUVqdXVtVUFCMDgyZ3c2dVptc2dndnQzTjdIRE9VLUM3MXMySDlfY2FqQkFfbmZyVGI2WkZIc0VyN2VmSTF1TEVqYXdNTEY4TDU2MHRlajlxem1mX29ta1p4NW1jUnBsZUQ4UjkyN1hPaWpzekpiYzV1bldQTi0tT1h3MVdLd28tR1FSY0pXVE9mTnV1WGlxNzlVM0lDLVdhYW5uQjhpckE1aVBoZ0hNb3hJLUlMdjZs0gG-AUFVX3lxTFBzYVVYZnBpQnFlMEFUQ3RCb2NrMERyQkhGQ1VCM0lIWm5zaXM5QkV6S2ZlQnpmNHZmNHROSXE1eHZYQ21waVFCVHJpZVd0c3BaQ3ZQUFduRkdlS1psczc5MXp5TWZOcDZmN2cwZlNDM185Y0hQbWtYcDlURk14TnhSeExrVm1NVndyRFJpcTRKVUNpOUsyTG9FejhMeEJ6WnpVRm05M0lKT3c1OEV5Nk84dUdGcDFmLXZTQnFZMmc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTE1TTTkyVGppeko1WEFvMmEzamUxWU9rVzBaOEh6MklzRUhjRUVaWkJidHEweHFXTDcyT2dERWt4ZDV6bG9hSVdvVWtrTXpLcVRqZjhBVUVNZ2hqdkct?oc=5&quot;&gt;International Crisis Group&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxOMHdqckFXeU5Pc0hXUmNvR0Q2LUx1Y29Mdkh0V2VpbUh0Y3MyR2NDb2t3UTRkVkoycU5yUTBQckllc1VGeHhyeFhsOWFxaVo